1
00:00:00,346 --> 00:00:02,949
What's today's video about?

2
00:00:03,276 --> 00:00:06,784
A comparison conversation. Which one do you prefer?

3
00:00:07,337 --> 00:00:08,837
Scene 1: Choosing Clothes by Size and Color

4
00:00:08,837 --> 00:00:11,470
Take a look.

5
00:00:11,493 --> 00:00:15,326
This shirt is so cute!

6
00:00:15,349 --> 00:00:18,416
It really is!

7
00:00:18,439 --> 00:00:22,476
We have it in red and blue.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:25,439
Which one do you like?

9
00:00:25,462 --> 00:00:31,411
Hmm... I prefer the blue one.

10
00:00:31,435 --> 00:00:33,938
I see.

11
00:00:33,961 --> 00:00:38,994
The blue one is a little bigger than the red one.

12
00:00:39,017 --> 00:00:41,957
You're right.

13
00:00:41,981 --> 00:00:45,514
The blue one is size L.

14
00:00:45,537 --> 00:00:48,915
The red one is size M.

15
00:00:48,938 --> 00:00:52,672
I think M fits me better.

16
00:00:52,695 --> 00:00:56,928
Then the red one would be better, right?

17
00:00:56,951 --> 00:01:02,418
But I love the color of the blue one more.

18
00:01:02,441 --> 00:01:04,781
Yeah, I agree.

19
00:01:04,805 --> 00:01:07,982
Which one is cheaper?

20
00:01:08,005 --> 00:01:11,105
Let's check the price.

21
00:01:11,128 --> 00:01:15,195
The blue one is 3,000 yen.

22
00:01:15,218 --> 00:01:18,051
How much is the red one?

23
00:01:18,074 --> 00:01:22,147
The red one is 2,500 yen.

24
00:01:22,171 --> 00:01:26,238
The red one is cheaper than the blue one.

25
00:01:26,261 --> 00:01:30,527
True, but I'm still torn.

26
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:35,323
Saki, what colors do you usually wear?

27
00:01:35,347 --> 00:01:39,780
I usually wear black or white.

28
00:01:39,803 --> 00:01:44,310
Then the red one would be a nice, bright change for you.

29
00:01:44,334 --> 00:01:46,568
Yeah, I agree.

30
00:01:46,591 --> 00:01:50,224
Red is such an energetic color.

31
00:01:50,247 --> 00:01:54,187
Yeah, I think it would look great on you.

32
00:01:54,210 --> 00:01:59,204
But I also love the cool tone of the blue one.

33
00:01:59,227 --> 00:02:02,327
Want to try them on?

34
00:02:02,350 --> 00:02:05,347
Yes, let's do that.

35
00:02:05,371 --> 00:02:08,642
Let's call a store clerk.

36
00:02:08,666 --> 00:02:12,381
There's a clerk over there.

37
00:02:12,404 --> 00:02:17,271
Excuse me, can I try this on?

38
00:02:17,294 --> 00:02:20,685
Sure, go ahead.

39
00:02:20,708 --> 00:02:23,741
The fitting room is over there.

40
00:02:23,764 --> 00:02:26,398
Which one will you try first?

41
00:02:26,421 --> 00:02:29,988
I'll try the red one first.

42
00:02:30,012 --> 00:02:33,359
Then the blue one after.

43
00:02:33,382 --> 00:02:35,518
Sounds good.

44
00:02:35,541 --> 00:02:39,574
Let's see which one suits you best!

45
00:02:39,597 --> 00:02:42,067
Thank you.

46
00:02:42,091 --> 00:02:45,191
Take your time.

47
00:02:45,214 --> 00:02:49,047
No rush, take it easy.

48
00:02:49,070 --> 00:02:51,570
I'm excited!

49
00:02:51,593 --> 00:02:53,093
Scene 2: Choosing Lunch Options

50
00:02:53,093 --> 00:02:56,760
I'm getting hungry.

51
00:02:56,782 --> 00:03:00,816
Me too. Let's grab something to eat.

52
00:03:00,839 --> 00:03:04,638
Shall we go into this restaurant?

53
00:03:04,662 --> 00:03:07,395
Sounds good.

54
00:03:07,418 --> 00:03:10,576
Let's check the menu.

55
00:03:10,599 --> 00:03:15,932
We have a meat lunch and a fish lunch.

56
00:03:15,955 --> 00:03:19,023
Which one would you prefer?

57
00:03:19,047 --> 00:03:24,914
I like both meat and fish.

58
00:03:24,938 --> 00:03:27,973
Me too.

59
00:03:27,997 --> 00:03:30,540
It's hard to decide.

60
00:03:30,564 --> 00:03:34,479
The meat lunch is 1,000 yen.

61
00:03:34,503 --> 00:03:38,936
The fish lunch is 800 yen.

62
00:03:38,959 --> 00:03:42,492
The fish lunch is cheaper.

63
00:03:42,515 --> 00:03:47,689
Yes, but the meat lunch is more filling.

64
00:03:47,713 --> 00:03:50,083
Yeah, I agree.

65
00:03:50,106 --> 00:03:54,206
I want to eat a lot today.

66
00:03:54,229 --> 00:03:58,096
Then, should we go with the meat lunch?

67
00:03:58,119 --> 00:04:03,652
Hmm, but the fish looks delicious too.

68
00:04:03,675 --> 00:04:07,951
This restaurant is famous for its fish.

69
00:04:07,974 --> 00:04:11,124
Really?

70
00:04:11,147 --> 00:04:15,181
Then, I think I'll go with the fish.

71
00:04:15,204 --> 00:04:21,917
The most popular dish on the menu is the fish lunch.

72
00:04:21,941 --> 00:04:25,841
In that case, I'll have the fish.

73
00:04:25,864 --> 00:04:28,897
I'll have the meat. I had fish at home yesterday.

74
00:04:28,920 --> 00:04:33,513
I had fish at home yesterday.

75
00:04:33,536 --> 00:04:36,322
I see.

76
00:04:36,346 --> 00:04:40,283
I hope the meat lunch is delicious too.

77
00:04:40,306 --> 00:04:42,773
I'm sure it will be.

78
00:04:42,796 --> 00:04:46,764
Oh, let's choose our drinks too.

79
00:04:46,787 --> 00:04:50,367
We have coffee and tea.

80
00:04:50,391 --> 00:04:54,291
I'd like some iced tea.

81
00:04:54,314 --> 00:04:58,467
There's tea on the menu too.

82
00:04:58,490 --> 00:05:01,045
It's 100 yen.

83
00:05:01,069 --> 00:05:03,735
Great!

84
00:05:03,758 --> 00:05:06,834
Then, I'll have the tea, please.

85
00:05:06,857 --> 00:05:11,174
I'll have coffee after my meal.

86
00:05:11,198 --> 00:05:13,752
Sounds good.

87
00:05:13,775 --> 00:05:17,809
Shall we call the waiter?

88
00:05:17,832 --> 00:05:22,023
Excuse me, may we order, please?

89
00:05:22,046 --> 00:05:27,523
One fish lunch and one meat lunch, please.

90
00:05:27,547 --> 00:05:32,980
And one tea and one coffee, please.

91
00:05:33,003 --> 00:05:34,503
Scene 3: Preferences for Seasons

92
00:05:34,503 --> 00:05:39,437
The weather is lovely today, isn't it?

93
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:44,393
Yes, the breeze feels great.

94
00:05:44,416 --> 00:05:48,950
Spring is my favorite season.

95
00:05:48,974 --> 00:05:55,607
Really? Is spring your favorite time of the year?

96
00:05:55,630 --> 00:06:01,863
Yes, it's warm and the flowers are beautiful.

97
00:06:01,886 --> 00:06:08,005
I prefer autumn over spring.

98
00:06:08,029 --> 00:06:10,495
Why is that?

99
00:06:10,518 --> 00:06:14,475
Autumn is cool too.

100
00:06:14,499 --> 00:06:18,833
And the food is delicious.

101
00:06:18,856 --> 00:06:23,766
True. The fruits are amazing.

102
00:06:23,790 --> 00:06:28,739
Which do you prefer, summer or winter?

103
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:34,748
Hmm, I think I prefer summer.

104
00:06:34,771 --> 00:06:40,204
Really? Summer is so hot.

105
00:06:40,227 --> 00:06:45,794
Yes, but I can swim in the ocean.

106
00:06:45,817 --> 00:06:53,550
I prefer winter over summer. Isn’t it too cold, though?

107
00:06:53,573 --> 00:06:59,051
It is cold, but I get to see the snow.

108
00:06:59,075 --> 00:07:02,263
Snow is so beautiful, isn’t it?

109
00:07:02,286 --> 00:07:07,153
There’s no snow in my country.

110
00:07:07,176 --> 00:07:09,843
Really?

111
00:07:09,866 --> 00:07:14,904
What’s the hottest time of the year?

112
00:07:14,927 --> 00:07:19,236
July is the hottest.

113
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:23,493
It’s over 30 degrees every day.

114
00:07:23,516 --> 00:07:26,830
That sounds tough.

115
00:07:26,853 --> 00:07:34,605
Yeah. That’s why spring in Japan is absolutely the best.

116
00:07:34,629 --> 00:07:36,896
That’s great!

117
00:07:36,919 --> 00:07:41,462
Are you going anywhere this weekend?

118
00:07:41,486 --> 00:07:46,391
Yes, I’m heading to the park to see the cherry blossoms.

119
00:07:46,414 --> 00:07:48,804
Sounds good.

120
00:07:48,827 --> 00:07:51,960
Who are you going with?

121
00:07:51,983 --> 00:07:55,131
I’m going with my friends.

122
00:07:55,155 --> 00:07:58,788
Are you bringing a packed lunch?

123
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:02,847
Yes, I’ll make plenty!

124
00:08:02,871 --> 00:08:05,538
That sounds like fun!

125
00:08:05,561 --> 00:08:09,241
Make sure to show me the photos!

126
00:08:09,264 --> 00:08:13,242
Of course, I’ll take lots!

127
00:08:13,265 --> 00:08:16,175
Hope the weather’s nice.

128
00:08:16,199 --> 00:08:20,108
Yeah, I think it’ll be sunny.

129
00:08:20,131 --> 00:08:21,631
Scene 4: How to Get to the Art Museum

130
00:08:21,631 --> 00:08:26,998
Let’s go to the art museum this Saturday.

131
00:08:27,021 --> 00:08:29,487
Sounds good.

132
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:32,882
How do we get there?

133
00:08:32,906 --> 00:08:37,006
We can take the train or the bus.

134
00:08:37,029 --> 00:08:40,129
Which is more convenient?

135
00:08:40,152 --> 00:08:44,618
The train is faster than the bus.

136
00:08:44,641 --> 00:08:47,991
How long does it take?

137
00:08:48,015 --> 00:08:52,148
About 30 minutes by train.

138
00:08:52,171 --> 00:08:55,204
What about the bus?

139
00:08:55,227 --> 00:08:59,369
The bus takes an hour.

140
00:08:59,392 --> 00:09:03,626
The train is way faster!

141
00:09:03,649 --> 00:09:10,115
Yeah, but the bus is cheaper than the train.

142
00:09:10,138 --> 00:09:12,572
How much is it?

143
00:09:12,595 --> 00:09:16,261
The bus is 200 yen.

144
00:09:16,284 --> 00:09:19,518
The train is 500 yen.

145
00:09:19,541 --> 00:09:23,207
That’s quite a difference.

146
00:09:23,230 --> 00:09:27,068
Yeah, which do you prefer?

147
00:09:27,091 --> 00:09:31,233
I’d rather take the cheaper option.

148
00:09:31,257 --> 00:09:35,336
Then should we go by bus?

149
00:09:35,359 --> 00:09:39,871
But the roads get really crowded on Saturdays.

150
00:09:39,894 --> 00:09:42,773
Oh, right.

151
00:09:42,797 --> 00:09:46,154
It’ll take even longer.

152
00:09:46,178 --> 00:09:51,611
In that case, maybe the train is better.

153
00:09:51,634 --> 00:09:53,901
Got it.

154
00:09:53,924 --> 00:09:57,257
Let’s take the train.

155
00:09:57,281 --> 00:10:00,714
Should we meet at the station?

156
00:10:00,737 --> 00:10:04,840
Yes, what time should we meet?

157
00:10:04,864 --> 00:10:08,781
The art museum opens at ten.

158
00:10:08,804 --> 00:10:11,571
How about nine?

159
00:10:11,594 --> 00:10:14,433
That works for me.

160
00:10:14,457 --> 00:10:18,642
Let's meet at nine at the station ticket gate.

161
00:10:18,665 --> 00:10:22,298
Where should we have lunch?

162
00:10:22,321 --> 00:10:27,034
There's a great place near the museum.

163
00:10:27,058 --> 00:10:31,558
Would you prefer a restaurant or a café?

164
00:10:31,581 --> 00:10:35,481
A café would be quieter and nicer.

165
00:10:35,504 --> 00:10:37,902
Sounds good.

166
00:10:37,926 --> 00:10:40,992
I'm really looking forward to it.

167
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:43,653
Me too.

168
00:10:43,676 --> 00:10:45,176
Scene 5: Tokyo vs. Countryside – Comparing Urban and Rural Life

169
00:10:45,176 --> 00:10:49,310
What's life in Tokyo like?

170
00:10:49,333 --> 00:10:54,881
It's fun, but it's so crowded.

171
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:57,570
Yeah, I agree.

172
00:10:57,593 --> 00:11:01,565
The trains are packed every day.

173
00:11:01,589 --> 00:11:07,540
My town is much quieter than Tokyo.

174
00:11:07,564 --> 00:11:10,554
What's your town like?

175
00:11:10,578 --> 00:11:15,680
The mountains are beautiful, and the air is so fresh.

176
00:11:15,703 --> 00:11:18,413
Sounds good.

177
00:11:18,437 --> 00:11:23,987
Which do you prefer—Tokyo or your hometown?

178
00:11:24,010 --> 00:11:26,948
I like both.

179
00:11:26,971 --> 00:11:32,084
But my town is more relaxing.

180
00:11:32,108 --> 00:11:35,642
How about shopping?

181
00:11:35,665 --> 00:11:42,617
Shopping is more convenient in Tokyo than in my town.

182
00:11:42,641 --> 00:11:46,951
There are so many stores.

183
00:11:46,974 --> 00:11:49,007
I'm sure it will be.

184
00:11:49,030 --> 00:11:54,530
But prices are higher in Tokyo.

185
00:11:54,553 --> 00:11:59,253
I think rent is the most expensive in Tokyo too.

186
00:11:59,276 --> 00:12:02,243
That's very true.

187
00:12:02,266 --> 00:12:06,366
Rent is cheaper in my town.

188
00:12:06,389 --> 00:12:10,022
How about the food?

189
00:12:10,045 --> 00:12:13,479
Which has better food?

190
00:12:13,502 --> 00:12:18,568
Vegetables taste better in my town.

191
00:12:18,591 --> 00:12:21,625
They're fresher.

192
00:12:21,648 --> 00:12:25,914
But Tokyo has way more restaurants.

193
00:12:25,937 --> 00:12:28,171
I'm sure it will be.

194
00:12:28,194 --> 00:12:33,028
You can try food from all over the world.

195
00:12:33,051 --> 00:12:37,084
That's one of Tokyo's best things.

196
00:12:37,107 --> 00:12:42,808
Why don't you come visit my town on your next day off?

197
00:12:42,832 --> 00:12:45,103
Oh,

198
00:12:45,126 --> 00:12:47,393
Really? That would be great!

199
00:12:47,416 --> 00:12:49,649
I'm sure it will be.

200
00:12:49,672 --> 00:12:54,706
I'll show you around by car.

201
00:12:54,728 --> 00:12:57,228
I'd love that!

202
00:12:57,251 --> 00:12:59,585
Thank you.

203
00:12:59,608 --> 00:13:05,342
We'll go to the best ramen shop in town.

204
00:13:05,365 --> 00:13:09,319
I love ramen!

205
00:13:09,343 --> 00:13:12,649
I think you'll really like it.

206
00:13:12,673 --> 00:13:15,908
Are there any hot springs?

207
00:13:15,931 --> 00:13:18,164
I'm sure it will be.

208
00:13:18,187 --> 00:13:22,820
There's a great hot spring near the mountains.

209
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:25,743
I'm excited!

210
00:13:25,766 --> 00:13:28,433
I can't wait to go!

211
00:13:28,456 --> 00:13:33,013
Let's go this weekend, then.

212
00:13:33,036 --> 00:13:34,903
I'm sure it will be.

213
00:13:34,926 --> 00:13:37,870
Looking forward to it!

214
00:13:37,893 --> 00:13:39,393
Scene 6: Fruit Picking 101 – How to Choose the Best Fruits

215
00:13:39,393 --> 00:13:42,141
Welcome!

216
00:13:42,164 --> 00:13:45,274
Would you like some fruit?

217
00:13:45,298 --> 00:13:50,398
The fruit at this supermarket looks so fresh!

218
00:13:50,421 --> 00:13:52,454
I'm sure it will be.

219
00:13:52,477 --> 00:13:57,510
Apples and oranges are on sale today!

220
00:13:57,533 --> 00:14:02,479
Which is sweeter, apples or oranges?

221
00:14:02,503 --> 00:14:07,742
Oranges are sweeter this time of year.

222
00:14:07,765 --> 00:14:10,341
I see.

223
00:14:10,364 --> 00:14:13,598
How about the apples?

224
00:14:13,622 --> 00:14:18,888
Apples are a little tart, but they're delicious.

225
00:14:18,911 --> 00:14:22,485
Hmm, which should I choose?

226
00:14:22,509 --> 00:14:26,046
We have samples available!

227
00:14:26,069 --> 00:14:28,536
Go ahead and try some.

228
00:14:28,559 --> 00:14:31,066
Thank you.

229
00:14:31,089 --> 00:14:34,956
I'll try the apple first.

230
00:14:34,979 --> 00:14:37,158
How is it?

231
00:14:37,181 --> 00:14:41,491
It's crisp and really tasty!

232
00:14:41,515 --> 00:14:45,615
Now try the orange.

233
00:14:45,638 --> 00:14:47,753
I'm sure it will be.

234
00:14:47,776 --> 00:14:52,013
Oh, the orange is sweeter!

235
00:14:52,037 --> 00:14:54,504
Right?

236
00:14:54,527 --> 00:14:59,793
This is the sweetest variety of orange we have.

237
00:14:59,816 --> 00:15:05,883
Both are delicious, but I prefer oranges.

238
00:15:05,906 --> 00:15:09,873
How many oranges would you like?

239
00:15:09,896 --> 00:15:14,367
My family will eat them too, so I'd like quite a few.

240
00:15:14,390 --> 00:15:17,940
This bag has ten oranges in it.

241
00:15:17,963 --> 00:15:20,663
I'll take that, please.

242
00:15:20,686 --> 00:15:23,123
How much is it?

243
00:15:23,146 --> 00:15:26,079
That'll be 500 yen.

244
00:15:26,102 --> 00:15:29,059
Do you have bananas too?

245
00:15:29,082 --> 00:15:31,049
I'm sure it will be.

246
00:15:31,073 --> 00:15:33,458
They're over there.

247
00:15:33,482 --> 00:15:38,677
Bananas are the cheapest fruit here, aren't they?

248
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:40,867
Yes, they are.

249
00:15:40,890 --> 00:15:44,271
They're great for eating every day.

250
00:15:44,294 --> 00:15:48,481
Okay, I'll take a bunch of bananas too.

251
00:15:48,504 --> 00:15:51,171
Thank you.

252
00:15:51,194 --> 00:15:54,977
Your total comes to 700 yen.

253
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,900
I'm sure it will be.

254
00:15:56,923 --> 00:15:59,623
Here's 1,000 yen.

255
00:15:59,646 --> 00:16:03,146
Your change is 300 yen.

256
00:16:03,169 --> 00:16:05,737
Thank you very much!

257
00:16:05,761 --> 00:16:08,307
I'll be back!

258
00:16:08,330 --> 00:16:11,034
We look forward to seeing you again!

259
00:16:11,058 --> 00:16:12,558
Scene 7: Favorite and Skilled Sports

260
00:16:12,558 --> 00:16:18,058
Did you watch any sports on TV on Sunday?

261
00:16:18,081 --> 00:16:22,666
Yes, I watched a soccer match.

262
00:16:22,689 --> 00:16:26,022
I watched baseball.

263
00:16:26,045 --> 00:16:29,181
It was really exciting!

264
00:16:29,205 --> 00:16:34,082
Which do you like better, soccer or baseball?

265
00:16:34,105 --> 00:16:38,338
I like baseball better.

266
00:16:38,361 --> 00:16:43,715
I prefer soccer over baseball.

267
00:16:43,739 --> 00:16:46,272
Why's that?

268
00:16:46,295 --> 00:16:52,328
Soccer players run a lot, so it looks really cool.

269
00:16:52,351 --> 00:16:54,658
I see.

270
00:16:54,682 --> 00:17:00,015
Baseball rules are a little more complicated, aren't they?

271
00:17:00,038 --> 00:17:02,371
Yeah, I agree.

272
00:17:02,394 --> 00:17:07,261
I don't really understand the rules.

273
00:17:07,284 --> 00:17:11,856
What sport are you best at?

274
00:17:11,879 --> 00:17:16,589
I'm best at tennis.

275
00:17:16,612 --> 00:17:19,193
Tennis, huh?

276
00:17:19,217 --> 00:17:21,584
Sounds good.

277
00:17:21,607 --> 00:17:26,540
I often play tennis at the park on weekends.

278
00:17:26,563 --> 00:17:29,396
Who would you like to play with?

279
00:17:29,419 --> 00:17:32,853
I'll play with my friends from work.

280
00:17:32,876 --> 00:17:35,785
That sounds like fun!

281
00:17:35,808 --> 00:17:39,643
I want to play sports too.

282
00:17:39,667 --> 00:17:44,433
Then how about playing tennis together this time?

283
00:17:44,456 --> 00:17:49,390
I'm not very good at tennis, is that okay?

284
00:17:49,413 --> 00:17:52,046
That's fine.

285
00:17:52,069 --> 00:17:55,302
I'll teach you slowly.

286
00:17:55,325 --> 00:17:57,625
I'd appreciate that.

287
00:17:57,648 --> 00:18:03,245
For exercising, which is better, morning or afternoon?

288
00:18:03,269 --> 00:18:07,624
Morning is better because it's cooler.

289
00:18:07,647 --> 00:18:09,881
Got it.

290
00:18:09,904 --> 00:18:14,204
Then let's do it on Sunday morning.

291
00:18:14,227 --> 00:18:18,293
Do we need any equipment?

292
00:18:18,316 --> 00:18:22,073
I can lend you a racket and shoes.

293
00:18:22,097 --> 00:18:24,168
That would be a big help.

294
00:18:24,191 --> 00:18:27,824
I'll bring some drinks.

295
00:18:27,847 --> 00:18:29,921
I'd appreciate that.

296
00:18:29,945 --> 00:18:33,330
Sports drinks would be great.

297
00:18:33,354 --> 00:18:35,824
Got it.

298
00:18:35,847 --> 00:18:38,280
I'll buy some and bring them.

299
00:18:38,303 --> 00:18:41,682
I'm really looking forward to Sunday.

300
00:18:41,706 --> 00:18:43,972
I'm sure it will be.

301
00:18:43,995 --> 00:18:46,341
I'll do my best.

302
00:18:46,365 --> 00:18:47,865
Scene 8: Evening Tea Time

303
00:18:47,865 --> 00:18:52,498
Dinner was really delicious, wasn't it?

304
00:18:52,521 --> 00:18:57,271
Yes, I'm so full.

305
00:18:57,294 --> 00:19:00,234
Would you like something to drink?

306
00:19:00,258 --> 00:19:03,358
I'll boil some water.

307
00:19:03,381 --> 00:19:05,921
I'd appreciate that.

308
00:19:05,945 --> 00:19:10,338
Which would you prefer, coffee or tea?

309
00:19:10,361 --> 00:19:16,230
Hmm, since it's nighttime, tea would be better.

310
00:19:16,253 --> 00:19:20,222
Does coffee keep you awake?

311
00:19:20,246 --> 00:19:25,236
Yes, coffee is better in the morning.

312
00:19:25,259 --> 00:19:27,367
Got it.

313
00:19:27,391 --> 00:19:30,059
I'll make some tea.

314
00:19:30,082 --> 00:19:34,349
Do you have sugar and milk?

315
00:19:34,372 --> 00:19:37,039
Yes, I do.

316
00:19:37,062 --> 00:19:39,615
Would you like both in your tea?

317
00:19:39,638 --> 00:19:43,622
Just milk for me, please.

318
00:19:43,646 --> 00:19:46,679
Sure, go ahead.

319
00:19:46,702 --> 00:19:50,069
It's hot, so be careful.

320
00:19:50,092 --> 00:19:52,625
Thank you.

321
00:19:52,648 --> 00:19:55,548
It smells wonderful.

322
00:19:55,572 --> 00:20:00,325
I got this tea as a souvenir.

323
00:20:00,349 --> 00:20:03,545
Which country is it from?

324
00:20:03,568 --> 00:20:06,274
England.

325
00:20:06,297 --> 00:20:10,197
England is famous for its tea, isn't it?

326
00:20:10,220 --> 00:20:13,412
It's really delicious.

327
00:20:13,435 --> 00:20:18,469
It has a nicer aroma than the tea from my country.

328
00:20:18,492 --> 00:20:20,967
I'm glad you like it.

329
00:20:20,990 --> 00:20:24,094
I also have some cookies.

330
00:20:24,118 --> 00:20:27,185
Wow, that's great!

331
00:20:27,208 --> 00:20:29,508
Let's dig in.

332
00:20:29,531 --> 00:20:34,441
What's your favorite drink?

333
00:20:34,464 --> 00:20:38,797
I like tea the most.

334
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:41,854
Japanese green tea?

335
00:20:41,877 --> 00:20:47,543
Yes, green tea goes best with sweet snacks.

336
00:20:47,566 --> 00:20:49,718
Yeah, I agree.

337
00:20:49,742 --> 00:20:53,575
I love green tea too.

338
00:20:53,598 --> 00:20:58,232
How about visiting a great tea shop together soon?

339
00:20:58,255 --> 00:21:01,155
Sounds good.

340
00:21:01,178 --> 00:21:05,244
There's a new one near the station.

341
00:21:05,267 --> 00:21:07,901
When should we go?

342
00:21:07,924 --> 00:21:11,492
How about this Saturday?

343
00:21:11,515 --> 00:21:14,790
Yes, I'm free.

344
00:21:14,814 --> 00:21:17,281
Let's go!

345
00:21:17,304 --> 00:21:19,937
I'm really looking forward to it!

346
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,460
Scene 9: Favorite Pets – Dogs and Cats

347
00:21:21,460 --> 00:21:24,037
Take a look.

348
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:28,775
That dog over there is so cute, isn't it?

349
00:21:28,798 --> 00:21:31,665
It really is!

350
00:21:31,688 --> 00:21:35,321
It's full of energy and runs around a lot.

351
00:21:35,344 --> 00:21:39,731
Do you have any pets?

352
00:21:39,755 --> 00:21:42,055
I'm sure it will be.

353
00:21:42,078 --> 00:21:46,211
I have two cats at home.

354
00:21:46,234 --> 00:21:48,807
Sounds good.

355
00:21:48,831 --> 00:21:53,364
Which do you prefer, dogs or cats?

356
00:21:53,387 --> 00:21:57,655
I like cats better.

357
00:21:57,679 --> 00:22:00,412
Why is that?

358
00:22:00,435 --> 00:22:07,582
They're quiet. Dogs can be a little noisy.

359
00:22:07,605 --> 00:22:12,272
I prefer dogs over cats.

360
00:22:12,295 --> 00:22:16,562
You can play with dogs, right?

361
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:18,493
I'm sure it will be.

362
00:22:18,517 --> 00:22:22,750
I take mine for a walk every morning.

363
00:22:22,773 --> 00:22:26,673
Dogs need walks.

364
00:22:26,696 --> 00:22:29,862
Cats don't need walks.

365
00:22:29,886 --> 00:22:33,273
Which is easier to keep?

366
00:22:33,296 --> 00:22:37,529
I think cats are easier to take care of.

367
00:22:37,552 --> 00:22:42,220
I'd love to have a big dog.

368
00:22:42,244 --> 00:22:49,828
Big dogs eat way more than small ones, you know.

369
00:22:49,851 --> 00:22:53,830
They cost a lot to keep.

370
00:22:53,854 --> 00:22:58,687
What's your favorite animal?

371
00:22:58,710 --> 00:23:03,424
I love horses the most.

372
00:23:03,447 --> 00:23:05,947
Horses?

373
00:23:05,970 --> 00:23:09,103
Can you ride them?

374
00:23:09,126 --> 00:23:11,226
I'm sure it will be.

375
00:23:11,249 --> 00:23:14,719
I learned when I was a kid.

376
00:23:14,742 --> 00:23:17,576
That's so cool!

377
00:23:17,599 --> 00:23:21,499
I like rabbits.

378
00:23:21,522 --> 00:23:24,630
Rabbits are cute too.

379
00:23:24,654 --> 00:23:26,931
Yes, they are.

380
00:23:26,954 --> 00:23:30,987
They're small and so fluffy.

381
00:23:31,010 --> 00:23:35,189
How about going to the zoo sometime?

382
00:23:35,213 --> 00:23:37,754
Sounds good.

383
00:23:37,777 --> 00:23:41,610
I'd love to see lots of animals.

384
00:23:41,633 --> 00:23:45,567
Pandas are the most popular, you know.

385
00:23:45,590 --> 00:23:48,456
I really want to see them!

386
00:23:48,479 --> 00:23:51,819
Let's take lots of pictures.

387
00:23:51,843 --> 00:23:56,395
Okay, let's go next Sunday.

388
00:23:56,418 --> 00:23:58,690
I'm sure it will be.

389
00:23:58,714 --> 00:24:01,947
I'll make some bento to bring along.

390
00:24:01,970 --> 00:24:04,804
Thank you.

391
00:24:04,827 --> 00:24:06,327
Scene 10: Choosing a Summer Vacation Destination

392
00:24:06,327 --> 00:24:10,325
Summer vacation is just around the corner!

393
00:24:10,349 --> 00:24:12,182
I'm sure it will be.

394
00:24:12,205 --> 00:24:15,838
Are you planning to go anywhere?

395
00:24:15,861 --> 00:24:19,161
I haven't decided yet.

396
00:24:19,184 --> 00:24:21,818
I'm still thinking about it.

397
00:24:21,841 --> 00:24:26,280
Would you rather go to the beach or the mountains?

398
00:24:26,303 --> 00:24:30,499
I'd prefer the beach.

399
00:24:30,523 --> 00:24:33,756
What do you want to do at the beach?

400
00:24:33,779 --> 00:24:36,846
I want to go swimming.

401
00:24:36,869 --> 00:24:40,805
And I really want to eat some fish.

402
00:24:40,828 --> 00:24:45,585
I prefer the mountains over the sea.

403
00:24:45,609 --> 00:24:48,126
Why is that?

404
00:24:48,149 --> 00:24:52,103
It's cooler in the mountains, after all.

405
00:24:52,127 --> 00:24:54,794
Yeah, I agree.

406
00:24:54,817 --> 00:24:59,350
The sea in summer is so hot.

407
00:24:59,373 --> 00:25:04,089
Camping in the mountains is the most fun!

408
00:25:04,112 --> 00:25:06,612
Camping, huh?

409
00:25:06,635 --> 00:25:08,943
Sounds good.

410
00:25:08,966 --> 00:25:12,701
The stars are beautiful at night.

411
00:25:12,725 --> 00:25:17,191
But there are so many bugs, though.

412
00:25:17,214 --> 00:25:19,348
I'm sure it will be.

413
00:25:19,371 --> 00:25:24,337
Which has more bugs, the sea or the mountains?

414
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:28,294
I think the mountains have more.

415
00:25:28,317 --> 00:25:31,794
Yeah, that might be true.

416
00:25:31,817 --> 00:25:37,789
What was your favorite place during your travels in Japan?

417
00:25:37,813 --> 00:25:42,880
Hokkaido was the best for me.

418
00:25:42,903 --> 00:25:47,136
The food in Hokkaido is amazing, isn't it?

419
00:25:47,159 --> 00:25:49,493
I'm sure it will be.

420
00:25:49,515 --> 00:25:52,873
The seafood bowls were absolutely incredible.

421
00:25:52,897 --> 00:25:57,281
I really want to go to Hokkaido now.

422
00:25:57,304 --> 00:26:00,204
Did you fly there?

423
00:26:00,227 --> 00:26:02,661
I'm sure it will be.

424
00:26:02,684 --> 00:26:07,265
Flying is faster than taking the Shinkansen.

425
00:26:07,288 --> 00:26:11,430
How much does a flight cost?

426
00:26:11,454 --> 00:26:16,320
Tickets get expensive during summer vacation.

427
00:26:16,343 --> 00:26:20,727
Which is more expensive, the Shinkansen or a flight?

428
00:26:20,751 --> 00:26:25,457
I think flights are probably pricier.

429
00:26:25,481 --> 00:26:27,781
Got it.

430
00:26:27,804 --> 00:26:31,147
I'll think about it.

431
00:26:31,170 --> 00:26:34,870
Hope you have a fantastic summer vacation!

432
00:26:34,893 --> 00:26:37,669
Thanks! I appreciate it.

433
00:26:47,700 --> 00:26:49,200
Scene 11: Moving and the Perks of My New Apartment

434
00:26:49,200 --> 00:26:53,136
You must be exhausted after moving. Good job!

435
00:26:53,159 --> 00:26:55,477
Thank you.

436
00:26:55,500 --> 00:27:00,167
Did you finally finish unpacking?

437
00:27:00,190 --> 00:27:04,490
Yeah, I finished everything yesterday.

438
00:27:04,513 --> 00:27:08,046
How do you like your new place?

439
00:27:08,069 --> 00:27:13,569
It's not as spacious as my old apartment.

440
00:27:13,592 --> 00:27:16,459
Really?

441
00:27:16,482 --> 00:27:21,415
Yeah, I got rid of a lot of stuff I didn’t need.

442
00:27:21,438 --> 00:27:26,305
Isn’t it inconvenient having a smaller place?

443
00:27:26,328 --> 00:27:31,661
Not at all. It’s closer to the station than my old place.

444
00:27:31,684 --> 00:27:35,517
How many minutes is it on foot?

445
00:27:35,540 --> 00:27:39,290
About five minutes.

446
00:27:39,314 --> 00:27:42,547
That’s super convenient!

447
00:27:42,570 --> 00:27:48,604
Yeah, my daily commute has become so much easier.

448
00:27:48,627 --> 00:27:52,693
Any other improvements?

449
00:27:52,716 --> 00:27:57,707
The windows are bigger, so the room is much brighter now.

450
00:27:57,731 --> 00:28:01,276
That’s wonderful!

451
00:28:01,299 --> 00:28:06,046
My old place was always so dark.

452
00:28:06,070 --> 00:28:09,703
Is there a supermarket nearby?

453
00:28:09,726 --> 00:28:14,042
There’s a big one right in front of the station.

454
00:28:14,066 --> 00:28:17,966
Shopping must be so easy now.

455
00:28:17,989 --> 00:28:23,489
Yeah, I can buy fresh vegetables every day.

456
00:28:23,512 --> 00:28:27,645
Cooking must be more fun now!

457
00:28:27,668 --> 00:28:33,101
It is! I’ve started cooking at home on weekends.

458
00:28:33,124 --> 00:28:38,291
Can I come visit your new place sometime?

459
00:28:38,314 --> 00:28:42,547
Of course! Please do come.

460
00:28:42,570 --> 00:28:46,712
I’ll pick up some delicious cake for you.

461
00:28:46,736 --> 00:28:49,519
I’m really looking forward to it.

462
00:28:49,542 --> 00:28:53,309
How about next Sunday?

463
00:28:53,332 --> 00:28:57,448
Yes, the afternoon works for me.

464
00:28:57,472 --> 00:29:01,150
I’ll call you when I arrive at the station.

465
00:29:01,173 --> 00:29:02,673
Scene 12: The Benefits of Exercise and How to Keep It Up

466
00:29:02,673 --> 00:29:07,739
Have you been exercising lately?

467
00:29:07,762 --> 00:29:10,911
Not at all.

468
00:29:10,935 --> 00:29:14,471
You should really get some exercise.

469
00:29:14,494 --> 00:29:16,963
Yeah, I agree.

470
00:29:16,987 --> 00:29:20,738
I’ve gained a little weight recently.

471
00:29:20,761 --> 00:29:26,502
I walk around my neighborhood every day.

472
00:29:26,526 --> 00:29:28,885
Walking, you mean?

473
00:29:28,908 --> 00:29:31,146
I'm sure it will be.

474
00:29:31,170 --> 00:29:35,315
I walk for about 30 minutes every morning.

475
00:29:35,339 --> 00:29:39,005
Wouldn’t jogging be better?

476
00:29:39,028 --> 00:29:44,895
Walking is just as effective as jogging, you know.

477
00:29:44,918 --> 00:29:47,784
Really?

478
00:29:47,807 --> 00:29:50,592
I didn’t know that.

479
00:29:50,616 --> 00:29:52,250
I'm sure it will be.

480
00:29:52,273 --> 00:29:56,573
The key is not to overdo it.

481
00:29:56,596 --> 00:29:59,380
That’s true.

482
00:29:59,403 --> 00:30:05,337
You can walk longer than you can run, so it’s easier to keep up.

483
00:30:05,360 --> 00:30:10,072
Maybe I could do that after all.

484
00:30:10,095 --> 00:30:13,395
You should definitely start!

485
00:30:13,418 --> 00:30:16,605
You’ll feel so much lighter.

486
00:30:16,629 --> 00:30:20,862
I’ll try walking tomorrow morning.

487
00:30:20,885 --> 00:30:24,798
Do you have proper walking shoes?

488
00:30:24,822 --> 00:30:28,255
I only have regular shoes.

489
00:30:28,278 --> 00:30:32,234
Your feet might hurt.

490
00:30:32,257 --> 00:30:36,010
I should get some proper sports shoes.

491
00:30:36,033 --> 00:30:40,575
Want to go shopping for some after work today?

492
00:30:40,599 --> 00:30:42,638
I'm sure it will be.

493
00:30:42,662 --> 00:30:47,132
I’ll look for something light and easy to walk in.

494
00:30:47,155 --> 00:30:51,122
Hope you find a great pair!

495
00:30:51,145 --> 00:30:53,417
Thank you.

496
00:30:53,440 --> 00:30:56,506
I’ll do my best starting tomorrow!

497
00:30:56,529 --> 00:31:00,364
Let’s get healthier together!

498
00:31:00,388 --> 00:31:06,262
Once you get used to walking, how about hiking with me?

499
00:31:06,286 --> 00:31:08,626
Sounds good.

500
00:31:08,649 --> 00:31:11,549
I’m really looking forward to it!

501
00:31:11,572 --> 00:31:16,105
I’ll keep it up for at least a month.

502
00:31:16,128 --> 00:31:19,062
I’ll be cheering you on!

503
00:31:19,085 --> 00:31:20,585
Scene 13: Deciding Whether to Upgrade Your Smartphone

504
00:31:20,585 --> 00:31:26,579
I’m torn about whether to upgrade my smartphone.

505
00:31:26,602 --> 00:31:30,702
Is your current phone old?

506
00:31:30,725 --> 00:31:36,258
Yes, I’ve had it for three years now.

507
00:31:36,281 --> 00:31:43,189
The new models have much better cameras than the old ones.

508
00:31:43,213 --> 00:31:48,724
Yeah, the photos come out so much clearer.

509
00:31:48,748 --> 00:31:53,857
Is your current phone acting up?

510
00:31:53,880 --> 00:32:01,580
It’s just not as convenient as the newer models.

511
00:32:01,603 --> 00:32:05,752
Does the battery die quickly?

512
00:32:05,775 --> 00:32:12,454
Yeah, I have to charge it twice a day.

513
00:32:12,478 --> 00:32:16,311
That sounds tough.

514
00:32:16,334 --> 00:32:24,034
The screen is crisp, the photos are great—I really want a new one.

515
00:32:24,057 --> 00:32:28,795
But new smartphones are expensive.

516
00:32:28,819 --> 00:32:35,386
Yeah, I’m hoping the price will drop a little.

517
00:32:35,409 --> 00:32:41,326
I don’t find the current model too inconvenient, though.

518
00:32:41,349 --> 00:32:46,282
If it’s just for calls and emails, it’s fine.

519
00:32:46,305 --> 00:32:49,172
Do you play games?

520
00:32:49,195 --> 00:32:55,232
Yes, I play for about an hour every day.

521
00:32:55,255 --> 00:33:01,755
In that case, you’d better get a high-performance smartphone.

522
00:33:01,778 --> 00:33:06,612
I’m thinking of checking some out at the electronics store this weekend.

523
00:33:06,634 --> 00:33:10,468
Mind if I come with you?

524
00:33:10,491 --> 00:33:14,424
Of course! Let’s look together.

525
00:33:14,447 --> 00:33:19,992
There are so many colors for smartphones these days, aren’t there?

526
00:33:20,015 --> 00:33:24,549
I’m looking for a blue one.

527
00:33:24,572 --> 00:33:29,356
We’ll need to buy a case too, won’t we?

528
00:33:29,379 --> 00:33:34,882
There’s an accessories shop next to the electronics store.

529
00:33:34,906 --> 00:33:38,498
Then let’s go there too.

530
00:33:38,521 --> 00:33:42,878
How about this Saturday afternoon?

531
00:33:42,901 --> 00:33:48,291
Sure, let’s meet in front of the station.

532
00:33:48,314 --> 00:33:51,624
Looking forward to it!

533
00:33:51,648 --> 00:33:53,148
Scene 14: Planning a Trip and Choosing Destinations

534
00:33:53,148 --> 00:33:58,248
Let’s discuss our long weekend trip.

535
00:33:58,271 --> 00:34:00,465
Sounds good.

536
00:34:00,489 --> 00:34:03,756
Where do you want to go?

537
00:34:03,778 --> 00:34:09,212
Would you prefer Kyoto or Osaka?

538
00:34:09,235 --> 00:34:13,868
I’d rather go to Kyoto.

539
00:34:13,891 --> 00:34:16,358
Why's that?

540
00:34:16,381 --> 00:34:21,314
I want to see old temples and shrines.

541
00:34:21,337 --> 00:34:26,104
Kyoto’s scenery is so beautiful.

542
00:34:26,127 --> 00:34:30,960
Yes, I want to take lots of photos.

543
00:34:30,983 --> 00:34:35,934
I want to eat lots of delicious food.

544
00:34:35,957 --> 00:34:41,624
You can eat amazing food in Osaka.

545
00:34:41,647 --> 00:34:45,965
Takoyaki and okonomiyaki are famous there.

546
00:34:45,988 --> 00:34:52,501
Yes, Osaka is a lively and fun city.

547
00:34:52,525 --> 00:34:58,297
How long does it take by train from Osaka to Kyoto?

548
00:34:58,320 --> 00:35:02,554
About 30 minutes by train.

549
00:35:02,577 --> 00:35:06,967
Then we can visit both!

550
00:35:06,990 --> 00:35:13,124
Right. It’s better to book a hotel in Osaka.

551
00:35:13,147 --> 00:35:15,580
Why's that?

552
00:35:15,603 --> 00:35:20,903
You can stay out late, and it’s cheaper too.

553
00:35:20,926 --> 00:35:24,042
That’s a great idea!

554
00:35:24,066 --> 00:35:30,569
Let’s sightsee in Kyoto during the day and eat in Osaka at night.

555
00:35:30,592 --> 00:35:35,382
That sounds perfect. I can’t wait to go!

556
00:35:35,406 --> 00:35:40,443
I’ll book the hotel online tonight.

557
00:35:40,466 --> 00:35:45,333
Please do. I’ll pay half.

558
00:35:45,356 --> 00:35:50,554
Got it. I’ll buy the Shinkansen tickets too.

559
00:35:50,577 --> 00:35:55,371
Thanks! Let’s start preparing for the trip.

560
00:35:55,394 --> 00:35:58,364
Hope the weather’s nice.

561
00:35:58,388 --> 00:36:01,931
What souvenirs should we buy?

562
00:36:01,955 --> 00:36:06,021
I’m planning to buy some traditional Japanese sweets.

563
00:36:06,044 --> 00:36:08,911
I’ll do the same.

564
00:36:08,935 --> 00:36:10,435
Scene 15: Tips for Improving Japanese Skills

565
00:36:10,435 --> 00:36:15,469
How’s your Japanese study going lately?

566
00:36:15,492 --> 00:36:19,192
I’m working hard every day.

567
00:36:19,215 --> 00:36:24,148
My Japanese has improved a lot compared to six months ago.

568
00:36:24,171 --> 00:36:26,968
Thank you.

569
00:36:26,992 --> 00:36:30,093
I’m so happy about that!

570
00:36:30,116 --> 00:36:34,351
Have you been practicing conversations a lot?

571
00:36:34,375 --> 00:36:36,609
I'm sure it will be.

572
00:36:36,632 --> 00:36:41,265
I try to speak with my Japanese friends.

573
00:36:41,289 --> 00:36:45,555
That’s the best way to practice!

574
00:36:45,578 --> 00:36:51,012
But kanji aren't as easy as grammar.

575
00:36:51,035 --> 00:36:55,604
Kanji are tough to memorize, aren't they?

576
00:36:55,627 --> 00:36:57,984
I'm sure it will be.

577
00:36:58,008 --> 00:37:03,308
Even if I learn to read them, I forget them so quickly.

578
00:37:03,331 --> 00:37:07,565
You should practice writing them a lot.

579
00:37:07,588 --> 00:37:09,821
Yes, they are.

580
00:37:09,844 --> 00:37:13,818
I'll write in my notebook every day.

581
00:37:13,841 --> 00:37:17,620
Can you understand the news on TV?

582
00:37:17,644 --> 00:37:21,024
It's still too difficult for me.

583
00:37:21,047 --> 00:37:25,435
I hope you can read the news soon!

584
00:37:25,459 --> 00:37:27,592
I'm sure it will be.

585
00:37:27,615 --> 00:37:31,715
You'll be able to read without using a dictionary.

586
00:37:31,738 --> 00:37:36,038
Watching anime is great for studying too.

587
00:37:36,061 --> 00:37:40,961
Isn't the Japanese in anime a little too fast?

588
00:37:40,984 --> 00:37:46,684
It is fast, but it helps with everyday conversation.

589
00:37:46,707 --> 00:37:51,304
I'll try watching Japanese anime this weekend.

590
00:37:51,328 --> 00:37:55,294
There are so many interesting anime out there!

591
00:37:55,317 --> 00:38:00,351
I'll look up words I don't know right away.

592
00:38:00,374 --> 00:38:05,951
Keep at it a little every day from now on, okay?

593
00:38:05,974 --> 00:38:08,141
I'm sure it will be.

594
00:38:08,164 --> 00:38:11,708
I want to pass the winter test.

595
00:38:11,732 --> 00:38:15,499
The N4 test, right?

596
00:38:15,522 --> 00:38:18,155
I’ll be cheering you on!

597
00:38:18,178 --> 00:38:23,511
If there's anything I don't understand, I'll ask you again.

598
00:38:23,534 --> 00:38:26,128
Of course!

599
00:38:26,152 --> 00:38:29,219
Let's study together.

600
00:38:29,242 --> 00:38:32,343
Looking forward to it!

601
00:38:32,367 --> 00:38:33,867
Scene 16: Telecommuting – The Pros and Cons

602
00:38:33,867 --> 00:38:38,235
Do you telecommute often these days?

603
00:38:38,258 --> 00:38:43,837
Yes, I work from home three times a week.

604
00:38:43,860 --> 00:38:48,494
Which do you prefer, going to the office or telecommuting?

605
00:38:48,517 --> 00:38:53,017
I prefer telecommuting.

606
00:38:53,040 --> 00:38:58,540
No commute, and I can sleep in—it's great!

607
00:38:58,562 --> 00:39:03,503
Yeah, the morning train is so exhausting.

608
00:39:03,527 --> 00:39:08,234
I'm always tired on days I go to the office.

609
00:39:08,258 --> 00:39:13,610
But don’t you find it hard to focus at home?

610
00:39:13,633 --> 00:39:19,008
I find it quieter at home and easier to concentrate.

611
00:39:19,032 --> 00:39:25,098
I think telecommuting isn’t as easy for discussions as going to the office.

612
00:39:25,121 --> 00:39:30,855
At the office, you can just ask the person next to you.

613
00:39:30,878 --> 00:39:36,511
Yeah, emailing questions takes so much time.

614
00:39:36,534 --> 00:39:40,101
How are online meetings for you?

615
00:39:40,124 --> 00:39:45,558
Sometimes the audio cuts out or the screen freezes.

616
00:39:45,581 --> 00:39:50,752
So it’s better to go to the office on meeting days.

617
00:39:50,776 --> 00:39:56,080
My company still doesn’t allow telecommuting.

618
00:39:56,103 --> 00:39:58,851
That sounds tough.

619
00:39:58,875 --> 00:40:01,751
You always go to the office?

620
00:40:01,774 --> 00:40:07,208
Yeah, I spend an hour on the train every day.

621
00:40:07,231 --> 00:40:11,864
Why not talk to your boss about telecommuting?

622
00:40:11,887 --> 00:40:14,189
Yeah, I agree.

623
00:40:14,213 --> 00:40:16,846
I’ll bring it up next time.

624
00:40:16,869 --> 00:40:22,342
On telecommuting days, you can make your own lunch.

625
00:40:22,366 --> 00:40:26,600
Eating out less means saving more money!

626
00:40:26,623 --> 00:40:30,895
I’m even more envious of telecommuting now.

627
00:40:30,918 --> 00:40:38,551
Work styles might gradually change next year. Fingers crossed!

628
00:40:38,574 --> 00:40:42,641
Want to grab a drink after work today?

629
00:40:42,663 --> 00:40:44,897
Sounds good.

630
00:40:44,920 --> 00:40:48,256
I’d love a cold beer!

631
00:40:48,279 --> 00:40:52,013
Let’s go to the izakaya near the station.

632
00:40:52,036 --> 00:40:53,536
Scene 17: Movies vs. Manga – A Comparison

633
00:40:53,536 --> 00:40:59,636
The movie just ended, didn't it?

634
00:40:59,658 --> 00:41:02,492
It was so intense and really fun to watch!

635
00:41:02,515 --> 00:41:06,615
The action scenes were incredible, right?

636
00:41:06,638 --> 00:41:10,671
Have you read the original manga?

637
00:41:10,694 --> 00:41:12,676
I'm sure it will be.

638
00:41:12,700 --> 00:41:17,255
The movie isn’t as detailed as the manga, though.

639
00:41:17,278 --> 00:41:22,011
Some important scenes were missing.

640
00:41:22,034 --> 00:41:27,567
But it’s only two hours long, so it can’t be helped.

641
00:41:27,590 --> 00:41:32,624
The movie has way more impact than the manga, though.

642
00:41:32,647 --> 00:41:38,613
I’m glad we got to see it on the big screen!

643
00:41:38,636 --> 00:41:42,803
It’s so much more moving than watching on TV.

644
00:41:42,827 --> 00:41:47,660
The music was just as amazing as the visuals.

645
00:41:47,683 --> 00:41:52,155
The new character voices fit perfectly.

646
00:41:52,179 --> 00:41:56,812
I definitely want to see the next movie in theaters too!

647
00:41:56,835 --> 00:42:02,215
The sequel is coming out next summer, apparently.

648
00:42:02,239 --> 00:42:06,431
Do we really have to wait a whole year?

649
00:42:06,455 --> 00:42:09,155
That’s so long...

650
00:42:09,178 --> 00:42:13,734
I’ll reread the manga in the meantime.

651
00:42:13,757 --> 00:42:18,498
I think I’ll reread all the volumes too.

652
00:42:18,522 --> 00:42:22,904
It’s always fun talking about our thoughts with friends.

653
00:42:22,928 --> 00:42:24,927
I'm sure it will be.

654
00:42:24,950 --> 00:42:28,617
I'm getting hungry.

655
00:42:28,640 --> 00:42:31,913
Should we grab dinner?

656
00:42:31,936 --> 00:42:36,456
I’m craving either hamburger steak or omurice.

657
00:42:36,480 --> 00:42:41,437
There’s a great Western-style restaurant just around the corner.

658
00:42:41,460 --> 00:42:44,250
Let’s go there!

659
00:42:44,274 --> 00:42:49,423
If we show our movie tickets, we get free drinks!

660
00:42:49,446 --> 00:42:52,980
That’s a great deal!

661
00:42:53,004 --> 00:42:55,637
Let's go!

662
00:42:55,660 --> 00:42:59,378
Let’s keep talking about the movie.

663
00:42:59,401 --> 00:43:01,268
I'm sure it will be.

664
00:43:01,291 --> 00:43:04,635
We can chat while we walk.

665
00:43:04,659 --> 00:43:06,159
Scene 18: The Benefits of Cooking at Home

666
00:43:06,159 --> 00:43:11,477
What do you usually do for lunch?

667
00:43:11,500 --> 00:43:18,200
I always grab a bento from the convenience store.

668
00:43:18,223 --> 00:43:24,365
I always bring a homemade lunch.

669
00:43:24,389 --> 00:43:28,255
You cook for yourself?

670
00:43:28,278 --> 00:43:30,812
That’s impressive!

671
00:43:30,835 --> 00:43:36,968
I love cooking, so it’s not a hassle at all.

672
00:43:36,991 --> 00:43:42,169
Which is better—eating out or cooking at home?

673
00:43:42,192 --> 00:43:48,136
Cooking at home is cheaper and healthier.

674
00:43:48,160 --> 00:43:53,026
I’d like to save a little money too.

675
00:43:53,049 --> 00:43:58,632
Then you should definitely start cooking for yourself!

676
00:43:58,656 --> 00:44:03,291
Vegetables have gotten so expensive lately.

677
00:44:03,314 --> 00:44:10,300
Yeah, but you don’t get as many veggies when eating out.

678
00:44:10,324 --> 00:44:15,991
Convenience store bentos don’t have much veggies either.

679
00:44:16,014 --> 00:44:21,916
If you cook at home, you can eat plenty of vegetables.

680
00:44:21,939 --> 00:44:28,125
Isn’t doing the dishes a pain when you cook at home?

681
00:44:28,148 --> 00:44:34,048
It’s a little annoying, but you get used to it and finish quickly.

682
00:44:34,071 --> 00:44:39,987
You can also prep meals in bulk on weekends and freeze them.

683
00:44:40,010 --> 00:44:44,544
Yeah, it doesn’t take much time on weekdays.

684
00:44:44,567 --> 00:44:50,467
Maybe I’ll try cooking a little starting tomorrow.

685
00:44:50,490 --> 00:44:53,390
That’s great!

686
00:44:53,413 --> 00:44:56,166
What are you going to make?

687
00:44:56,189 --> 00:45:01,723
I’ll start with the easiest thing—fried eggs!

688
00:45:01,746 --> 00:45:04,012
Sounds good.

689
00:45:04,035 --> 00:45:07,469
Perfect for breakfast!

690
00:45:07,492 --> 00:45:12,158
We need to buy a pot and a frying pan.

691
00:45:12,181 --> 00:45:16,766
Why don’t we pick them out together at the supermarket this weekend?

692
00:45:16,790 --> 00:45:19,177
Thank you.

693
00:45:19,201 --> 00:45:22,034
Looking forward to it!

694
00:45:22,057 --> 00:45:28,090
Cooking makes every day more fun!

695
00:45:28,113 --> 00:45:31,813
I can’t wait to get better at it.

696
00:45:31,836 --> 00:45:34,624
I’ll be cheering you on!

697
00:45:34,648 --> 00:45:37,015
Keep up the good work!

698
00:45:37,038 --> 00:45:41,671
Yes, I’ll make delicious meals!

699
00:45:41,694 --> 00:45:43,194
Scene 19: Comparing Seasonal Clothing

700
00:45:43,194 --> 00:45:47,261
It’s gotten cold all of a sudden, hasn’t it?

701
00:45:47,284 --> 00:45:53,150
Yeah, I need to bring out my winter clothes soon.

702
00:45:53,173 --> 00:45:58,355
Do you prefer winter clothes or summer clothes?

703
00:45:58,379 --> 00:46:03,545
I like winter better than summer.

704
00:46:03,568 --> 00:46:06,117
Why is that?

705
00:46:06,141 --> 00:46:11,853
Winter lets you layer all kinds of outfits.

706
00:46:11,876 --> 00:46:15,191
It’s so fun to play with fashion!

707
00:46:15,215 --> 00:46:20,248
Yeah, coats and scarves are so cute.

708
00:46:20,271 --> 00:46:27,771
Plus, I hate the heat, so I’m not a big fan of summer.

709
00:46:27,794 --> 00:46:32,927
I prefer summer clothes—they’re easier to wear.

710
00:46:32,950 --> 00:46:36,508
They’re so light, right?

711
00:46:36,532 --> 00:46:42,232
Yeah, and summer clothes are way easier to wash.

712
00:46:42,256 --> 00:46:46,689
Washing winter sweaters is such a hassle.

713
00:46:46,712 --> 00:46:51,045
Winter clothes cost more for dry cleaning too.

714
00:46:51,068 --> 00:46:56,426
Winter coats are as expensive as boots!

715
00:46:56,450 --> 00:46:58,950
Yeah, I agree.

716
00:46:58,973 --> 00:47:03,316
Department store clothes are so pricey.

717
00:47:03,339 --> 00:47:09,439
I always buy cheap clothes online.

718
00:47:09,462 --> 00:47:13,229
Doesn’t the sizing ever bother you?

719
00:47:13,252 --> 00:47:18,603
Sometimes, but I read the reviews carefully.

720
00:47:18,626 --> 00:47:22,960
They say this winter’s going to be especially cold.

721
00:47:22,983 --> 00:47:26,959
We should get some warm clothes.

722
00:47:26,982 --> 00:47:33,415
Yeah, we’ll need thick jackets to avoid catching a cold.

723
00:47:33,438 --> 00:47:37,940
Let’s get scarves and gloves ready too.

724
00:47:37,964 --> 00:47:43,431
Want to go shopping together this weekend?

725
00:47:43,454 --> 00:47:46,087
Sounds good.

726
00:47:46,110 --> 00:47:49,343
Let’s go to the mall in front of the station.

727
00:47:49,366 --> 00:47:54,039
I want to have some warm ramen for lunch.

728
00:47:54,062 --> 00:47:56,596
That sounds amazing!

729
00:47:56,619 --> 00:47:59,457
I'm really looking forward to it.

730
00:47:59,481 --> 00:48:03,398
Let’s set a budget before we go.

731
00:48:03,421 --> 00:48:04,921
Scene 20: Business Trip Transportation: Shinkansen or Airplane?

732
00:48:04,921 --> 00:48:11,655
Did you book your business trip ticket yet? I’m torn between the Shinkansen and a flight.

733
00:48:11,678 --> 00:48:14,781
Flights are faster.

734
00:48:14,804 --> 00:48:19,538
The Shinkansen isn’t as fast as a plane, though.

735
00:48:19,561 --> 00:48:25,930
True, but the Shinkansen is way more comfortable to ride.

736
00:48:25,954 --> 00:48:31,220
No need to check luggage or go through security.

737
00:48:31,243 --> 00:48:36,910
You can board the Shinkansen right after arriving at the station.

738
00:48:36,933 --> 00:48:41,124
No waiting around for procedures—nice!

739
00:48:41,147 --> 00:48:47,380
The Shinkansen has way more legroom than a plane.

740
00:48:47,403 --> 00:48:51,303
You can open your laptop and get work done.

741
00:48:51,327 --> 00:48:55,914
Yeah, I don’t want to waste travel time.

742
00:48:55,937 --> 00:48:59,671
Which one’s more expensive?

743
00:48:59,694 --> 00:49:06,060
The company’s paying, but the Shinkansen is a little cheaper.

744
00:49:06,083 --> 00:49:11,183
How long does it take to get to Tokyo on the Shinkansen?

745
00:49:11,206 --> 00:49:14,926
About four hours.

746
00:49:14,949 --> 00:49:18,083
This is quite a long trip, isn't it?

747
00:49:18,106 --> 00:49:20,703
Aren't you getting tired?

748
00:49:20,726 --> 00:49:26,359
Don't worry, we'll have a delicious bento lunch along the way!

749
00:49:26,382 --> 00:49:31,416
Train station bentos are so fun—there are so many varieties to choose from!

750
00:49:31,438 --> 00:49:37,178
Absolutely! That's the best part of traveling by Shinkansen.

751
00:49:37,202 --> 00:49:41,591
I love the view from airplanes, though.

752
00:49:41,615 --> 00:49:46,521
The scenery above the clouds is truly breathtaking.

753
00:49:46,544 --> 00:49:52,247
When traveling far, the best option really depends on the destination, doesn't it?

754
00:49:52,271 --> 00:49:57,904
Since the office is near the station, I decided to take the Shinkansen this time.

755
00:49:57,927 --> 00:50:02,446
I'll book the tickets online this afternoon.

756
00:50:02,470 --> 00:50:06,205
Hopefully, I can get a window seat!

757
00:50:06,228 --> 00:50:10,961
Yes! I want to reserve a seat where I can see Mount Fuji.

758
00:50:10,984 --> 00:50:14,417
Have a safe trip!

759
00:50:14,440 --> 00:50:16,611
Thank you.

760
00:50:16,635 --> 00:50:19,935
I'll bring back some souvenirs for you!